// =============================================================================
// Barracks — the drillmaster's troop-training menu (WO-453 troop-training flow).
// Opened by DialogueService.PlayStructure("barracks", "Barracks"), which routes the
// "barracks" structureId to THIS node (Barracks_MainMenu) — mirroring the pet-house
// PetHouse branch — instead of the generic StructureMenu.
//
// MINIMAL but working: a greeting + three options. Both panel-opening options use the
// COMMAND-FIRST pattern (the <<command>> is the FIRST content under the option, before
// any dialogue line) — a line BEFORE the command makes the Yarn VM pause on the line
// and the command never fires (the StructureMenu "Buy never opens" bug). "View Army"
// also opens the training panel (it shows the live owned counts + the army cap), so no
// new Yarn variable has to be declared/seeded just to print a count.
//
// Flavor is intentionally light — a richer drillmaster narrative is authored
// separately; this just needs to COMPILE in the Yarn project and FUNCTION.
//
// Custom commands used: <<ShowTrainingUI>> (no args) — registered ONCE on the shared
// DialogueRunner by DialogueCommandBridge. No new Yarn variables are introduced.
// =============================================================================
title: Barracks_MainMenu
tags: structure interaction barracks
---
Drillmaster: Looking to raise some soldiers? The Realm won't defend itself.

-> Train troops.
    // Command FIRST (mirrors the vendor nodes): a line before the command would make
    // the VM pause and <<ShowTrainingUI>> would never fire -> the panel never opens.
    <<ShowTrainingUI>>
    <<stop>>
-> Review my army.
    // Same panel — it lists every troop's owned count and the army cap at the top.
    <<ShowTrainingUI>>
    <<stop>>
-> Not today.
    Drillmaster: Then keep your blade close. The enemy doesn't rest.
===
